Package: hp-notebook-81ff-support
Architecture: all
Depends: convertible-power (>= 1.0.0), udev, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: thermald, smartmontools
Description: HP Notebook (board 81FF, Core i7-7500U) hardware support for Debian
 Settings for the HP Notebook with system board 81FF (product number
 1BQ18UA#ABA, Core i7-7500U, Realtek RTL8188EE wireless) on a stock Debian
 GNOME desktop: it pulls in convertible-power (maximum performance on AC,
 maximum battery life on battery) and adds this laptop's settings.  The main
 one stops the Realtek wireless adapter from flooding the kernel log with
 PCI Express errors, which loaded journald and the disk, by turning off PCI
 Express ASPM on the kernel command line (takes effect at the next boot).
 .
 The settings are applied only when the DMI board name is "81FF".
